<title>CHINA: China's red-chip companies make option debut in HK.</title>
<headline>China's red-chip companies make option debut in HK.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stock option trading on China Resources Enterprise Ltd and Shanghai Industrial Holdings Ltd started on Monday, The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong said.</p>
<p>Trading in Shanghai Industrial was particularly active with 831 contracts changing hands while 23 contracts were traded on China Resources, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Both stocks are the first non-Hang Seng Index constituent stocks to have introduced options on their shares and would provide more investment and risk management opportunities to investors, it said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
